 "reasons": [
  "N008 and N009 raised to level 2: neither is a case of 'Your Body Might Need Some Love First' (one is about any session stirring things up, the other about a self-hating reader's motive for coming); both are readiness items of their own.",
  "N018 Signs of Manipulation set one level below N017: it is the checklist for the warning N017 gives about following an outer adult.",
  "N136-N140 (finding a therapist, AI therapy) moved from the end of the real-life part to under N016 Borrow the Adult, after the outer-adult warnings: a therapist is a borrowed adult, the section says it is for first steps, and the real-life part's own intro sets therapists apart from 'real life other people'. N136 becomes level 3 and its four cases level 4. N017 stays directly after N016 because N016's last sentence runs into N017's heading.",
  "N043 and N044 moved up to sit right after N035-N039, so the Nurturer's spiritual material is together, the spiritual problem (N040) comes after all of it, and the vow (N041-N042) closes the Nurturer.",
  "N050 Timing Is Individual moved to first under the Guide: it is the readiness check (enough Nurturer and Protector first) and should come before the Guide's techniques.",
  "N070 merged into N069: single short child, and N069's last line ('Here's one trick from that article:') introduces it.",
  "N072 merged into N071: a 66-word single child that only continues N071 ('works the same way').",
  "N092 What to Do With a Peak moved after the safety cluster (N093-N100) and the author's too-soon story (N101): safety before what to do with a good outcome; its opener 'Now, the beautiful stuff' reads better after the warnings.",
  "N132 Taking a Break moved from Speaking Up and Handling Conflict to the end of Differentiation: its text is about differentiation and says the break may be needed 'even if they aren't doing anything to you', so it is not a conflict case.",
  "N145 Schema Therapy and N146 IFS set one level below N144 How This Relates to Similar Therapies: they are its two cases.",
  "The Love Has to Move (N135) now closes the real-life part, as its text does.",
  "Pointers checked: 'further on' in N012, N064, N078, N079 and the named references in N073, N092, N142, N137, N138, N147 all still point the right way. To recheck: N035 opens by referring back to the dog and the friend thought experiment in N032 (unchanged distance); N091 opens by continuing from the urge to escape in N087-N088 (unchanged)."
 ]
